Teach configure.ac about cross compiling to NetBSD.

CPython restricts cross builds to an explicit allowlist of hosts and errors
out with "cross build not supported for $host" on anything else:

    checking MACHDEP... configure: error: cross build not supported for
    x86_64-unknown-netbsd

Add a netbsd arm to the two host case statements, in the same shape as the
existing freebsd-cross.patch. Nothing else is needed: unlike Solaris, NetBSD
needs no MACHDEP normalisation entry, since the cross value ("netbsd") already
matches what the rest of the build expects.

--- a/configure.ac
+++ b/configure.ac
@@ -342,6 +342,9 @@
 	*-*-wasi*)
 	    ac_sys_system=WASI
 	    ;;
+	*-*-netbsd*)
+	    ac_sys_system=NetBSD
+	    ;;
 	*)
 		# for now, limit cross builds to known configurations
 		MACHDEP="unknown"
@@ -812,6 +815,9 @@
 	wasm32-*-* | wasm64-*-*)
 		_host_ident=$host_cpu
 		;;
+	*-*-netbsd*)
+		_host_ident=$host_cpu
+		;;
 	*)
 		# for now, limit cross builds to known configurations
 		MACHDEP="unknown"
